window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"kled","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Kled","Kled","Skill","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Your levels 2-3","text":"W attack speed plus the Q-root threat punishes every greedy trade — this is where the lane lead gets built."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"He learns to sidestep Q and the free window closes — land the tether or do not commit."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"Remount sustain plus bruiser stats re-open the gap — extended trades profit again."},{"when":"Side lanes late","text":"His healing and the Determination revive decide late duels — avoid the clean 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q tethers into W burst","Trade around his sidesteps","Take every side-lane duel late"],"foe":["Dodge your Q and trade clean","Keep level-6 fights even","Avoid the 1v1 you keep inviting"]},"early":"Even at 1, dominant at 2-3: once Violent Tendencies and the Bear Trap tether come online, Q-root into W burst punishes every greedy trade he takes. Push that advantage hard, because at 4-5 he learns to sidestep Q and pick clean trades — landed tethers stay mandatory, and coin-flip fights are not worth it.","mid":"Level 6 tilts to him — Grim Deliverance (R, 80-110s) heals him for a share of the damage it deals, so a clean fight is no longer a wash. Let his cooldowns pick your moments. First item evens it out: remount sustain and the bruiser spike make short trades profit, and a dive with jungle help is still clean.","late":"Two-plus items, straight side-lane duels are yours: R engage forces the fight on your terms and remount doubles your effective health mid-scrap. Split-push, drag him to you, and only respect the version of him that arrives with teammates — alone, he loses the duel.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm before your W and Q tether come online.","At level 2 your W attack speed and Q-root threat out-trade him.","Level 3 is yours — Q-root into W burst punishes his greedy trades.","The 4-5 window is even once he can sidestep Q and pick his trades cleanly.","Grim Deliverance (R) heals him through your burst, and his passive can revive him.","At first item your remount sustain and bruiser spike roughly match his.","Two items in, his Q and R healing plus the revive out-last your frontloaded burst."]});
